ount', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nRedJoker: 1, BlackJoker: 1, 2: 3, A: 2, K: 2, Q: 2, J: 1, 10: 3, 9: 2, 8: 3, 7: 1, 6: 1, 5: 1, 4: 1, 3: 2\nValid Moves:\nsingle: ♣9\nsingle: ♦J\nsingle: ♠Q\nsingle: ♦K\nsingle: ♣A\npass: []\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Evaluation: To beat ♥7 we can play a higher single. Promising options are:\n- ♣9: wins cheaply and keeps our high cards for later.\n- ♦J / ♠Q / ♦K / ♣A: also win, but spending these higher singles now is inefficient and may reduce our ability to stop the landlord later.\nPassing would give the lead to our teammate, but it also lets the landlord’s ♥7 stand and may allow them to keep control.\n\nReason: Play the smallest winning card (♣9) to take control at low cost, preserve our higher singles for key stops later, and potentially set up a better lead on our next play.\n\nAnswer: {"cards":["♣9"]}'}
